Z||000000||firstfiero||01-18-2001||12:36 PM||||   Any of you guys use it?The person who owned the car befor me used so I am to but I have a few questions? Does it really work better? Is it true I can never go back to regular oil again? Thanks 86se w/a 100000 miles on it..||||reg||1
Z||000001||kinboyatuwo||01-18-2001||01:38 PM||||YES!!!<BR>I switched two oil changes ago and it had made a difference.  The car feels better and runs smoother at high rpm.  It is well worth the extra money<P>If anyone is considering doing this switch do an engine flush before for the best results and most benifits <P>------------------<BR>"Friends don't let friends drive four doors."||||reg||5
Z||000002||stimpy||01-18-2001||02:39 PM||||A benefit of synthetic that I got to experience first hand is that if you throw a rod through your block after driving 400 miles in the middle of July averaging 80 mph, the oil does not catch on fire.  Saved my ayass.<P>Also, don't laugh, but the folks who have joined within the past year may not be aware of my little discovery. You can get a 5qt Mobil One, lube and filter change at Wal-Mart for $27. That's less then the cost of the oil.  Of course, check the work carefully when they are done.<P>------------------<BR>Loud Pipes Save Lives!      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/stimpy_sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||firstfiero||01-18-2001||02:45 PM||||   LOL...walmart is where I go also. Grease Monkey charges 30 bucks for a regular oil change. I don't want to know what they charge for synthetic!||||reg||1
Z||000004||terryk||01-18-2001||02:58 PM||||You can go back, sure, but the synthetic will clean much of the gunk out of the engine (after a few oil changes) and any places that are being sealed with gunk rather than a seal/gasket will leak.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000005||rogergarrison||01-18-2001||04:16 PM||||i used a little (qt@ 500-1,000) valvoline. switched to Castrol 5w50 full sythetic and it now goes clear to oil change without adding (5,000-7,000)||||reg||1
